{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790377452,"nonce":"Fx5RB7no05DrLvFBjdFd5ZOXRgc=","title":"Abstract field resolution (@:op(a.b) / @:resolve), arrayAccess by arity, `this` in inlined interpolation","message":"From the E0100 \"class not registered or field does not exist\" cluster in report-bx (686): 7 of 17 rows had an ABSTRACT receiver; of those, Issue3753/7981/9680/9758 (and 6017) use field resolution.\n\n- `@:op(a.b)` stringified through the Debug fallback of expr_to_string and `@:resolve` was never recorded, so no resolver was ever found; a field the abstract lacks reached MIR as a plain field read (E0100). Now both record as \"a.b\"; HIR rewrites `x.name` -\u003e `x.resolver(\"name\")` and `x.name = v` -\u003e `x.resolver(\"name\", v)` when the abstract has no member of that name. The resolver's result type feeds chained reads and binary-operator lookup (the TAST types such a field as a placeholder).\n- `op=` on an abstract's field was desugared in the TAST before HIR could find `@:op(a -= b)`; it is now kept for HIR, which desugars it itself when no overload exists.\n- An `@:op` formal of an abstract over String now accepts a String operand (Issue9758 `resolver * \"v\"` with `@:from String`).\n- A same-file `@:arrayAccess` method was matched only when named get/set; Haxe matches any name by arity (Issue7981 `resolve(key)`), which imported abstracts already did.\n- inline_expression_deep had no StringInterpolation arm: `'$this.$name'` inside an inlined abstract method lowered `this` unbound, and MIR silently dropped the rest of the caller (filed separately as 456a69c).\n\nProbes: scratch rs/Main.hx, C0-C2, D0-D4. Fixture: haxe-conformance/regressions/AbstractResolveOperators.hx.\n\nResult: report-by 688 (from 686), 0 LOST; GAINED Issue7981, Issue9758. MOVED Issue9680 COMPILE_FAIL -\u003e WRONG_ANSWER (needs type-level @:using); Issue3247 CRASH -\u003e WRONG_ANSWER (its @:arrayAccess `access` now matches; `e[2]++` does not apply @:op(A++) to an indexed value). Suite 206/0/2, fixtures and compiler integration tests green.\n\nStill failing: Issue3753 (resolvers C/D are MACRO functions; B is a static resolver), Issue9680 (type-level @:using), Issue6017 (utest Assert.same on PosInfos), Issue4327 (@:callable), Issue8200/6703 (method value from an interface receiver).","files":null}]}